 6 |     let $x: f64 set_to 0.5;
   |             ^^^
 what: `f64` says which kind of float it is: `.stable`, `.fast` or `.ieee`
 why:  a float always says its kind straight after its type, since floats differ between machines in nearly every other language (D257)
